      "problem": "A curve is defined as $y=3x-5.$ Find the average rate of change of $y$ over the interval $[3,7].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=3x-5.$ Applying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(7)-f(3)}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3(7)-5]-[3(3)-5]]}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16-4}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
